From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the cold hint skips placeholder addresses past the device address space (cerroverb, zortos293/Lichii #1568), unconditional

What: images at GPU addresses without memory get placeholder device addresses past the device
address space (~(1 << 40) + n in texture_cache.h). An upload to one is recorded in uploaded_ranges
like any other, and every 600 frames TextureCache::TickFrame hands each range to
DeviceMemoryManager::HintCold, which indexed tracked_entries at those pages: far outside the table
(ours has 2^36 bytes of device address space, so 2^24 pages). On another device that was a GPU-thread
crash (SIGSEGV in HintCold from TickFrame, about 4 min into another game; gone with the fix over
12 min). Nothing shows Ocarina hits it; a HintCold or TickFrame frame in one of our crash
backtraces would say so.

Now HintCold returns for a range that starts at or past 1 << AS_BITS and clips one that runs past
the end. Unconditional, no switch: for every range inside the address space the loop reads the
same pages as before and makes the same runs; only reads that were outside the table (undefined
behaviour: a crash or a junk physical address hinted cold) are skipped. No log line.

Origin and credit: cerroverb, zortos293/Lichii PR #1568 (open), commits 05beffd ("skip cold hints
for placeholder addresses") and d6cbce6 ("clamp the cold hint size in DAddr"); their final state,
applied as is.
---
diff --git a/src/core/device_memory_manager.inc b/src/core/device_memory_manager.inc
index a71bf02..265f11e 100644
--- a/src/core/device_memory_manager.inc
+++ b/src/core/device_memory_manager.inc
@@ -191,6 +191,15 @@ void DeviceMemoryManager<Traits>::HintCold(DAddr address, size_t size) {
         VAddr virtual_address; ///< 0: no CPU mapping known
         u64 size;
     };
+    // Images at GPU addresses without memory get placeholder addresses past the device address
+    // space (~(1 << 40) + n, texture_cache.h), which has no pages to look up: tracked_entries
+    // would be read far outside its table (cerroverb, zortos293/Lichii #1568). Skip a range that
+    // starts there, clip one that runs past the end.
+    constexpr DAddr address_space_end = DAddr{1} << AS_BITS;
+    if (address >= address_space_end) {
+        return;
+    }
+    size = static_cast<size_t>((std::min)(DAddr{size}, address_space_end - address));
     std::vector<Run> runs;
     const size_t page_end = Common::DivCeil(address + size, Memory::YUZU_PAGESIZE);
     for (size_t page = address >> Memory::YUZU_PAGEBITS; page < page_end; ++page) {
